{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAQjU1aM9smzzKhDPrE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job never reported because the failure notifier was silenced by the failure it was meant to report. Every run also failed for a separate reason, and I could only confirm the first one locally.\n\n**What's wrong**\n\n1. **zsh killed the notifier.** `status=$?` on line 19 of `nightly-review.zsh` fails because `status` is read-only in zsh. The script died there, so `notify.sh` never ran. I reproduced this with a stub `claude` that exits 1.\n2. **Every run failed on login.** The `.err` log has six \"Not logged in · Please run /login\" entries, one per run, matching `runs = 6`. The job fired on schedule every time. The plist sets only `PATH`, with no `USER`, so my best guess is that the headless `claude` can't reach its keychain login under launchd. I couldn't confirm that here; only a real launchd run will.\n3. **The notifier was an unverified silent path.** `notify.sh` calls `curl` without `-f`, and it sends an empty token if the keychain lookup fails. I couldn't confirm either from the logs, so I hardened it.\n\n**What I changed** (in the snapshot only)\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: `rc=$?` instead of `status`, `< /dev/null` on the `claude` call, failure on non-zero exit *or* empty output, and per-run exit/seconds/bytes logged to the `.out` file.\n- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER=vk` and `HOME=/Users/vk`. The account name comes from the paths in the plist, so change it if yours differs.\n- `bin/notify.sh`: exits with a message if the token is empty, and uses `curl -fsS`.\n\n**Verification:** the script passes `zsh -n`, the plist passes `plutil -lint`, and three stubbed cases behave correctly (failure, success, exit 0 with empty output). The notifier's token guard works. I did not contact Telegram, touch the real `claude` login, copy files into `~/bin` or `~/Library/LaunchAgents`, or load or kick the job. The stub tests don't prove `claude` works under launchd.\n\n**The colleague's note:** the `status` bug and the \"check the real outcome, not just the exit code\" point applied directly. The `USER` fix applies to the \"Not logged in\" error in these logs. The `< /dev/null` and \"Input must be provided\" stdin issue was not in these logs, so I added the redirect only as hardening.\n\nCauses, what applied from the note, and the steps to reload and verify are in `ANSWER.md`. Your next step is to copy the files into place and run `launchctl kickstart`, then check that the output file is fresh and the Telegram message arrives. The snapshot stops at 2026-10-18, so runs after that aren't covered here. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3898,"cache_read_input_tokens":38398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3898},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b84d48a4-a8ab-42e5-aa1a-14c5cd4f18cf","uuid":"b715749d-e3dc-4c53-9094-1fa842ba833a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:08:13.405Z","request_id":"req_011CgSAQjDPASgqv6rhAUKMS"}
